id: pm-8su89a
title: "Order workspace snapshot restores against claims without wall-clock time: bind each claim to a durable restore generation so a skewed restore clock cannot make a replaced claim look provable to --takeover-stale"
description: "The stale-claim takeover refuses when a workspace snapshot restore at or after the holder's claim may have replaced the holder's later work. The only order between the workspace stream and an item stream is wall-clock time, though. When the restoring host's clock runs behind the holder's, a restore that really happened after the claim carries an earlier timestamp, and the takeover then treats the restored claim as provable. A durable restore generation recorded on each claim would order the two without trusting clocks."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: claims,clock,takeover,workspace-snapshot
created_at: "2026-11-15T23:11:20.391Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T23:13:30.054Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Every workspace snapshot restore activation advances a durable restore generation; Claim history entries record the generation, and --takeover-stale refuses with workspace_restored when the claim's generation differs from the current one; A regression with a restore clock behind the claim clock refuses the takeover"
parent: pm-gh1357
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "A takeover refuses whenever a workspace restore activated after the holder's claim, whatever either host's clock says"
actual_result: "A restore stamped earlier than the claim by a lagging clock is ignored, so the restored claim looks provable"
dependencies[3]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
