  pm-vgk0nj,related,"2026-11-15T23:11:20.391Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
body: "## Observed\n\n`workspaceRestoredSince` (`src/sdk/ownership-source.ts`) compares each `workspace_snapshot_restore` record's `ts` (and a compacted workspace baseline's `last_activity_at`) with the anchor claim record's `ts`. `appendWorkspaceAuditEvent` stamps `nowIso()` without ordering it against item history.\n\nScenario (Codex review): a July 1 claim, July 4 work, then a restore of a July 1 snapshot whose host clock reads June 30. The restore record predates the claim by timestamp, so the July 1 claim survives as provable and a July 5 takeover is permitted over work the restore discarded.\n\n## Fix direction\n\n- Keep a durable, monotonically increasing restore generation in the tracker root, bumped by every restore activation.\n- Record the generation in the claim history entry's context. A takeover is provable only when the claim's generation equals the current one. Claims without the field are judged by today's timestamp rule, or refused once any restore exists.\n- This probably shares machinery with fenced claim generations (pm-gh1359) and with the root-swap fence (pm-vgk0nj).\n\nUntil then, the documented assumption stands: restore precedence uses wall-clock time, and the restoring host's clock must not run behind the holder's."
